    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353-a1">

                <pb facs="0508" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg426"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Telegram]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harvey S. Firestone to President
                    Coolidge</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Akron, Ohio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-04-30T12:19:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                                1925—12:19 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I am having difficulty in securing signature of Liberian Government to the rubber
                    planting agreements which were approved by the State Department. I am asking Mr.
                    W. R. Castle for assistance. Knowing your interest in this rubber development I
                    am taking liberty of advising you of the situation. Personal regards.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey S.
                    Firestone</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
